      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Very good race. COLLEANO (7) was runner-up two back at Bowen then sat deep throughout but kept coming and scored a determined win. Drops in weight and expected to go close again. TAMBO'S JUSTICE (2) is a lightly raced six-year-old with a great record here at home, and has never missed the frame from five starts this course and distance. Last start got home well when sixth in the rich Newmarket in Cairns. This is far easier and despite the big weight gets a chance to atone. CANBERRA LEGEND (6) tried to lead throughout and gave a huge sight but was grabbed late by COLLEANO. Looks hard to run down again with the light weight. AGED CARE (5) just missed in a similar race last time and looks tough to beat in this line-up. FREE CARRY (3) rates highly and will take catching.",
